doc:    "A line comment among the elements of a list that initialises a `const` is lifted out of the list — there is nowhere inside `[]` for it to be printed — and lands in the gap under the declaration. The first pass wrote it directly against the `];` above it and the mandatory blank line under it; the second pass read that gap back as one run above the *next* declaration, where the blank line goes above the run instead, so `format(format(x)) != format(x)` and the file was rewritten on every other run forever. Nothing was lost and nothing stopped parsing. Found by mutating a `const` of `Style` while the worked monorepo's interface library was being written. The same class as the doc-comment swap: a gap between two tokens printed in more than one piece, each piece internally canonical and the concatenation not. Here the pieces were the module's per-declaration sweep, which printed the stranded run with nothing above it, and the next declaration's own `decl_trivia`, which printed the blank line under it — and the next read of the file lexes that whole gap as one run above the next declaration, which comes back with the blank line above it. Fixed by deleting the sweep as an emission of its own: `Build::lead_trivia` drains the previous declaration's stranded comments together with the run written directly above this declaration and prints the lot through one `trivia_doc` call, which is what `Build::flush` already does for every gap that ends in a token. A stranded `///` is still left for the module's closing sweep, because printing it here would make it the next declaration's documentation. The printed shape is pinned by cli/tests/formatting/comment_stranded_in_a_list_lands_above_the_next_declaration/. No existing formatting golden moved."
oracle: "roundtrip"
status: FIXED
